      ],
      "text": "The project is Agents 2.0, a major update adding support for agent learning and evaluation, released 2024-06-25."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_0d36ab97baa7d137fc6cf2dd0f41cf1aef121c5cd38d17470636a0088f42aff5",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "design-choices",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59",
          "git_sha": "9896757a190d9742ce14229b32cd8ecaea8bcaa6",
          "line_end": 31,
          "line_start": 31,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "aiwaves-cn/agents",
          "url": "https://github.com/aiwaves-cn/agents/blob/e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59/README.md#L31-L31"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_761d0e98d86b70c35f865a8d87c36968696cdab58f17a0455a6f628c5e79c22f"
      ],
      "text": "Agent symbolic learning analogizes an agent pipeline to a neural net's computational graph, with prompts and tools playing the role of layer weights."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_10d38630123cb9ea5b3e2677a0704e49280dd570e1b9cf9ce24b1c567486d1f7",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59",
          "git_sha": "9896757a190d9742ce14229b32cd8ecaea8bcaa6",
          "line_end": 35,
          "line_start": 35,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "aiwaves-cn/agents",
          "url": "https://github.com/aiwaves-cn/agents/blob/e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59/README.md#L35-L35"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_41070abca667c6ac0c3f71357c3dd3455e5cb4cb4fbd564f4d394ba03e4d165b"
      ],
      "text": "Training implements a forward pass (agent execution) recording inputs, outputs, prompts, and tool usage per node in a trajectory, then a prompt-based loss producing a language loss."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_39f17a94648d3760f736674f93015db6b513f53bb61c484ae47ce9d94f1b0a18",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59",
          "git_sha": "9896757a190d9742ce14229b32cd8ecaea8bcaa6",
          "line_end": 35,
          "line_start": 35,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "aiwaves-cn/agents",
          "url": "https://github.com/aiwaves-cn/agents/blob/e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59/README.md#L35-L35"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_41070abca667c6ac0c3f71357c3dd3455e5cb4cb4fbd564f4d394ba03e4d165b"
      ],
      "text": "The framework back-propagates language loss along the trajectory to produce textual 'language gradients', then updates symbolic components and the node graph via prompts."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_e5e2f2a95e099f6a7e9ba6d256b0e6b0578a8638de3ed05fc6bb01ca3d60a58c",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "orchestration",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59",
          "git_sha": "9896757a190d9742ce14229b32cd8ecaea8bcaa6",
          "line_end": 35,
          "line_start": 35,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "aiwaves-cn/agents",
          "url": "https://github.com/aiwaves-cn/agents/blob/e8c4e3c2d19739d3dff59e577d1c97090cc15f59/README.md#L35-L35"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_41070abca667c6ac0c3f71357c3dd3455e5cb4cb4fbd564f4d394ba03e4d165b"
      ],
      "text": "The approach supports optimizing multi-agent systems by treating nodes as distinct agents or allowing multiple agents to act within one node."
    },
